>
  <h2>What the site itself does</h2>
  <p>Pages are HTML, CSS, and self-hosted fonts. There is no comment form, no account, and no MetricsPick analytics cookie. Fonts are served from this site’s own files. The pages do not request Google Fonts.</p>
  <p>A small inline script listens for clicks on links to datafa.st. When one is clicked, the script pushes an event named <code>affiliate_click</code> onto <code>window.dataLayer</code>, with the link URL, the visible link text, the current path, and a placement label such as <code>home-pick</code>.</p>
  <h2>Google Tag Manager</h2>
  <p>Every page loads Google Tag Manager container <code>GTM-PJ8GQK6B</code>. The container can read that dataLayer, including affiliate clicks, and send them to tags configured inside Tag Manager. Analytics such as GA4 are loaded through that container. This site does not embed a separate gtag.js snippet. What Tag Manager actually fires depends on the tags in the container, which are managed in Google’s interface rather than in this repository. Tag Manager may set cookies according to those tags.</p>
  <h2>Hosting and outbound links</h2>
  <p>The site is built to be hosted on Vercel. A host can see ordinary request logs, such as IP address and user agent, under its own policy. Outbound links to DataFast, Google, PostHog, Mixpanel, Amplitude, Plausible, and Fathom are subject to those companies’ sites once you leave. DataFast links are affiliate links, described on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions can go to the address on the <a href="/contact/">contact</a> page. That mailbox is the public editorial address for this new site and should be confirmed before you rely on a reply.</p>
</Simple>
